        "object": "<ul><li><p>German scrapes home 6-4, 3-6, 6-7 (7), 7-5, 6-4 in thriller</p></li><li><p>‘I think this is the longest first-round match I’ve played’</p></li></ul><p>Alexander Zverev rallied just in time to avoid becoming the first men’s No 1 seed to lose in the first round of a grand slam tournament since 2003, edging Lorenzo Sonego 6-4, 3-6, 6-7 (7), 7-5, 6-4 in a US Open match that ended in the early hours of Wednesday morning.</p><p>Zverev could not cash in on repeated chances to break Sonego’s serve for much of the night and was in danger of becoming the first top-seeded man to fall in his first match in a major tournament since Ivo Karlovic beat Lleyton Hewitt at Wimbledon in 2003.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/sep/02/alexander-zverev-survives-near-five-hour-marathon-us-open-tennis\">Continue reading...</a>"
